-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/f1849535-d107-5476-85a3-1a560f899a18
-- title:
--   Slope transfer for the twisted hyperbolic term
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $K$ and $L$ are number fields with $L/K$ finite Galois, $\sigma : L \simeq_K L$ is an automorphism such that every element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma^{-1}$ (hypothesis `hgen`), and $[L:K]$ is prime (`hdeg`). Real numbers $\alpha < \beta$ with $0 < \alpha$ cut out the idele-norm slab $\{g \mid \lVert \det g\rVert \in [\alpha,\beta]\}$, where the norm is [`NumberField.TateGlobal.ideleNorm`](def/NumberField_TateGlobalZeta.html#L19), i.e. the module of the idele acting on the adele ring.
--
--   *Global geometric data.* On the $L$-side, $\Phi_L$ is a subset of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ contained in that slab (`hΦs`) and a fundamental domain for the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ under `globalPoints` acting on the adelic Haar measure `adelicGLHaar` restricted to the slab (`hΦ`); $\nu_{Z,L}$ is a Haar measure on $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ and $\Omega_L$ a fundamental domain for the principal ideles (`hΩL`). The datum $D$ is an [`M4aHerbrand.IdeleGaloisDescent`](def/M4aHerbrand_IdeleClassVocab.html#L28): a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to the ring automorphisms of $\mathbb{A}_L$, continuous and compatible with the embedding of $L$. The same data $\Phi_K$ (`hΦKs`, `hΦK`), $\nu_{Z,K}$, $\Omega_K$ (`hΩK`) are given over $K$.
--
--   *Places and ramification.* $S_K$ and $S_L$ are finite sets of finite places of $K$ and of $L$ with: every place of $L$ above $S_K$ lies in $S_L$ (`hSL`); $S_L$ is a union of fibres of the map $w \mapsto w|_K$ (`hSsat`); and every place of $L$ whose restriction to $K$ avoids $S_K$ is unramified, `Ideal.ramificationIdx' = 1` (`hS`).
--
--   *Characters.* $\xi_L$ is a homomorphism from the full subgroup of $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$, continuous (`hξc`), trivial on principal ideles (`hξt`), taking the same value on $\det$ of the Hecke generators `heckeGen` at any two places outside $S_L$ lying over the same place of $K$ (`hξσ`), and invariant under the $\sigma^{-1}$-action of $D$ on ideles (`hξinv`). The finite set $\Xi$ of characters of $\mathbb{A}_K^\times$ is characterised by `hΞ`: $\xi \in \Xi$ exactly when $\xi$ is continuous, trivial on principal ideles, and satisfies $\xi \circ \mathrm{Nm} = \xi_L$ for the idelic norm of `genuineBaseChange`. By `hur`, each $\xi \in \Xi$ is unramified outside $S_K$: it kills local units of valuation $1$ at each $v \notin S_K$.
--
--   *Levels, types and test factors.* $N$ is an ideal of $\mathcal{O}_L$ all of whose prime divisors lie in $S_L$ (`hN`), $N'$ an ideal of $\mathcal{O}_K$ with prime divisors in $S_K$ (`hN'`); $\mathrm{tys}_L$, $\mathrm{tys}_K$ are archimedean type families. Fixed factors are $\varphi_a$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes \mathbb{R})$, $\varphi_S(v)$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$, $f_{a,K}$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(K \otimes \mathbb{R})$ and $f_{S,K}(v)$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$; $f_{a,K}$ is an archimedean test factor, i.e. given by a smooth function of the archimedean matrix entries and of compact support (`hfaK`), and each $f_{S,K}(v)$, $v \in S_K$, is locally constant of compact support (`hfSK`). A compact set $X$ of functions from the places of $L$ to $\mathbb{C}^2$ is given (`hXc`) containing the set of all $x$ vanishing on $S_L$ and satisfying, at each $w \notin S_L$, the three conditions $(x w)_2 = \mathrm{Nm}(w)\,\xi_L(\det \mathrm{heckeGen}_w)$, $\lVert (x w)_1\rVert \le (\mathrm{Nm}(w)+1)\lVert \xi_L(\det \mathrm{heckeGen}_w)\rVert^{1/2}$ and $\overline{(x w)_1} = \overline{(x w)_2}\,\lVert (x w)_2\rVert^{-1}(x w)_1$ (`hX`). Finally $c_0 \in \mathbb{C}$ is a constant.
--
--   *The geometric input `hgeo`.* For every finite $S' \supseteq S_K$, every continuous compactly supported $\varphi$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ which is unit-factorisable above $S'$ of type $\mathrm{tys}_L$ for the level `levelOne (𝓞 L) L N ⊓ finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup L`, every continuous compactly supported $f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ unit-factorisable at $S'$ of type $\mathrm{tys}_K$ for `principalLevel (𝓞 K) K N' ⊓ finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup K`, matching at $S'$ along $\sigma^{-1}$, and such that at each $v \notin S'$ unramified in $L$ the indicator of the semi-local integral set matches the indicator of the local integral set: the $\xi_L$-folded central integral over $\Omega_L$ and over $\Phi_L$ of the sum of $\varphi(x^{-1}\,\delta\,{}^{\sigma^{-1}}(z x))$ over those $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ whose twisted norm class `normClassMap hgen` is the conjugacy class of some $\gamma$ in the elliptic or the central cell of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$, equals $c_0$ times $\sum_{\xi_K \in \Xi}$ of the corresponding $\xi_K$-folded integral over $\Omega_K$ and $\Phi_K$ of `adelicKernelCentralPart` plus `adelicKernelEllipticPart` of $f$ at $(x, zx)$.
--
--   *Hecke data at auxiliary places.* $T$ is a finite set of places of $K$, disjoint from $S_K$ (`hTdisj`), with at least two elements (`hT2`), such that no place of $L$ above $T$ lies in $S_L$ (`hTSL`). For each place $v$ of $K$, $\mathrm{ws}\,v$ is a chosen place of $L$ above $v$, and $w'$ is a further assignment of places of $L$ satisfying $(w' v)\mathcal{O}_L = \sigma^{-1}\cdot(\mathrm{ws}\,v)\mathcal{O}_L$ for $v \in T$ (`hw'`). Upstairs, $\varpi_v$ are elements of the valuation ring at $\mathrm{ws}\,v$, irreducible and with non-zero image in the completion for $v \in T$ (`hϖirr`, `hϖs0`); $r_{T,v} : \mathrm{Fin}(n_v) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(L_{\mathrm{ws}\,v})$ is, for $v \in T$, a Hecke coset system for the integral subgroup and the diagonal element $\mathrm{diag}(\varpi_v,1)$, i.e. the representatives lie in the double coset, cover it modulo the integral subgroup, and are pairwise inequivalent (`hrTs`); and $z_v$ is the scalar matrix $\varpi_v \cdot 1$ (`hzs`). The data $\varpi_{K,v}$, $r_{K,v} : \mathrm{Fin}(n_{K,v}) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$, $z_{K,v}$ over $K$ satisfy the same conditions (`hϖKirr`, `hϖKs0`, `hrKs`, `hzKs`).
--
--   Under these hypotheses there exists a constant $\mathrm{lam} \in \mathbb{C}$ with the following property. Let $k, j$ be arbitrary functions from the places of $K$ to $\mathbb{N}$ (the Hecke word). Let $\varphi_L$ be continuous of compact support on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ and $\varphi_f$ a function on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{L,\mathrm{fin}})$ such that `IsSemiLocalFactorization K L (SK ∪ T)` holds for $\varphi_L$, $\varphi_a$, $\varphi_f$ and the semi-local family whose factor at $v \in T$ is $x \mapsto \sum_{\iota : \mathrm{Fin}(k_v) \to \mathrm{Fin}(n_v)}$ of the indicator of the semi-local integral set at $(\text{semi-local component of the local embedding of } \prod_m r_{T,v}(\iota m)\cdot z_v^{\,j_v})^{-1}x$, and whose factor at $v \notin T$ is $\varphi_S(v)$ (`hSLF`); thus $\varphi_a$ is an archimedean test factor, $\varphi_f$ a locally constant compactly supported finite factor, the listed factors are semi-local test functions on $S_K \cup T$, $\varphi_f$ is the product of those factors on elements integral outside $S_K \cup T$ and vanishes otherwise, and $\varphi_L$ is the product of $\varphi_a$ on the archimedean part and $\varphi_f$ on the finite part. Assume moreover that $\varphi_L$ is bi-invariant under `levelOne (𝓞 L) L N ⊓ finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup L` (`hbi`) and archimedean bi-finite of type $\mathrm{tys}_L$ (`harch`).
--
--   Let $\mathrm{fam}$ assign a function on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ to each slot index $m$, a dependent function sending $u \in T$ to an element of $\mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to_{0} \mathbb{N}$. Assume `hfam`: for every $m$ in `SatakeCombination.slotIndex K L ws k j T` — the finset of such $m$ whose value at each $v \in T$ lies in the support of `slotWord K L ws v (k v) (j v)` — the function $\mathrm{fam}\,m$ is bi-invariant under `principalLevel (𝓞 K) K N' ⊓ finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup K`, archimedean bi-finite of type $\mathrm{tys}_K$, the factors $f_{a,K}$ and $f_{S,K}$ again satisfy the test-factor conditions, and there is a locally constant compactly supported $f_f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{K,\mathrm{fin}})$ which, on elements whose components outside $S_K \cup T$ are integral, is the product over $v \in S_K \cup T$ of the factor $f_{S,K}(v)$ for $v \notin T$ and, for $v \in T$, of $x \mapsto \sum_{\iota : \mathrm{Fin}(m_v(0)) \to \mathrm{Fin}(n_{K,v})}$ of the indicator of the local integral set at $(\prod r_{K,v}(\iota m)\cdot z_{K,v}^{\,m_v(1)})^{-1}x$, which vanishes when some component outside $S_K \cup T$ is non-integral, and which satisfies $\mathrm{fam}\,m\,g = f_{a,K}(g_\infty)\,f_f(g_{\mathrm{fin}})$. Assume finally `hmatch`: $\varphi_L$ and $x \mapsto \sum_{m} c_{k,j}(m)\,\mathrm{fam}\,m\,x$ are matching at $S_K \cup T$ along $\sigma^{-1}$, where $c_{k,j}(m) =$ `SatakeCombination.slotFamilyCoeff K L ws k j T m`, the product over $v \in T$ of `slotCoeff` at $m_v$.
--
--   Then, for all complex numbers $A_L, B_L$, all functions $A_K, B_K$ assigning to a character of $\mathbb{A}_K^\times$ and a slot index a complex number, and all $R_0 \in \mathbb{R}$, the following holds. Suppose that for every $R \ge R_0$ both of the following two assertions are true.
--
--   First, the truncated twisted hyperbolic term upstairs is affine with slope $A_L$: the integral over $x$ in `canonicalTruncationDomain L α β` against `adelicGLHaar`, of the integral over $z \in \Omega_L$ against $\nu_{Z,L}$ of $\xi_L(z)$ times the difference of (i) the sum of $\varphi_L(x^{-1}\,\delta\,{}^{\sigma^{-1}}(z x))$ over those $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ whose twisted norm class is the conjugacy class of some $\gamma$ in the hyperbolic cell of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$, and (ii) the value at $z x$ of the indicator of the set where [`NumberField.AdelicHeight.adelicHeight L`](def/NumberField_AdelicHeight.html#L158) exceeds $e^{R}$ times the constant term — taken with the measure $\nu$ of `productionPinsOf L ΦL (levelOne ⊓ finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup) heckeGen (adelicBox L)`, namely additive adelic Haar measure conditioned on the adelic box, along the unipotent one-parameter subgroup `unipotentGL2` — of the function $y \mapsto \sum_{\delta} \varphi_L(x^{-1}\,\delta\,{}^{\sigma^{-1}}y)$ over the $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ with lower-left entry $0$ and $\mathrm{Nm}_{L/K}(\delta_{00}/\delta_{11}) \ne 1$, equals $R\,A_L + B_L$.
--
--   Second, for every $\xi_K \in \Xi$ and every slot index $m$, the corresponding truncated hyperbolic term downstairs is affine with slope $A_K(\xi_K,m)$: the integral over $x$ in `canonicalTruncationDomain K α β` of the integral over $z \in \Omega_K$ of $\xi_K(z)$ times the difference of `adelicKernelHyperbolicPart K (fam m) x (z x)` and the value at $z x$ of the indicator of the set where `adelicHeight K` exceeds $e^{R}$ times the constant term, for the analogous measure from `productionPinsOf K ΦK (principalLevel ⊓ finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup) heckeGen (adelicBox K)` and the unipotent subgroup, of $y \mapsto \sum_{\gamma} \mathrm{fam}\,m\,(x^{-1}\gamma y)$ over the $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ with lower-left entry $0$ and $\gamma_{00}/\gamma_{11} \ne 1$, equals $R\,A_K(\xi_K,m) + B_K(\xi_K,m)$.
--
--   The conclusion is the single identity
--   $$A_L = \mathrm{lam}\cdot \sum_{\xi_K \in \Xi}\ \sum_{m \in \mathrm{slotIndex}} c_{k,j}(m)\,A_K(\xi_K,m),$$
--   with the same $\mathrm{lam}$ for all Hecke words $(k,j)$, all admissible $\varphi_L$ and all matched ground families. The intercepts $B_L$ and $B_K$ are constrained only through the affineness hypotheses.
--
--   This is the slope half of the comparison of hyperbolic terms in the base-change trace formula for $\mathrm{GL}(2)$ over a cyclic extension of prime degree: the linear growth rate in the truncation parameter of the $\xi_L$-folded twisted hyperbolic term upstairs is one fixed multiple, independent of the Hecke word, of the Satake-combined growth rates of the hyperbolic terms of the matched ground families. It feeds the winding assembly [`AutomorphicForm.exists_const_forall_exists_windingDatum_sub_finrank_mul_const_mul_sum_eq_sum_mul_coeff_of_hyperbolicTerm_eq_affine`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_const_forall_exists_windingDatum_sub_finrank_mul_const_mul_sum_eq_sum_mul_coeff_of_hyperbolicTerm_eq_affine).
